{
  "name": "epanet_prv_network",
  "description": "A PRV holding 200 kPa static pressure at its outlet feeds a looped low-pressure zone beside a high zone: verifies the active PRV (static-pressure setpoint converted to EPANET's head setting) within a network against EPANET 2.2.",
  "source": "WNTR 1.5.0 EpanetSimulator (EPANET 2.2.0); see tests/reference/generate_epanet_cases.py. D-W headloss, GPM INP units, accuracy 1e-5, headerror 1e-9 ft and flowchange 1e-12 gpm (EPANET reads both in the INP units, input1.c:595-596; WNTR writes them unconverted); viscosity VISCOS = 1.1e-5 ft2/s = 1.02193344e-6 m2/s (the project's custom fluid has the same nu; its density, 1000 kg/m3, does not affect the comparison because friction depends only on nu and a surface-pressure head p/(rho g) is converted with the same rho and g on both sides); solver run in 'swamee_jain' mode. Known EPANET biases, all far inside the 0.5% criterion: EPANET's head-loss coefficients use g = 32.2 ft/s2 = 9.81456 m/s2 against our 9.80665 (0.08% in head loss), its minor-loss constant is 0.02517 against the exact 1/(2g(pi/4)^2) = 0.0251730 in US units (0.012%), its GPM flow-unit constant GPMperCFS = 448.831 differs from the exact ft3/(gal/60) by -3.8e-07 (relative, in flow), and its results are float32 (about 1e-7 relative). PRV/PSV: EPANET's setting is a head above the node elevation without velocity head, ours a static pressure at the valve port, so the generator iterates setting = p_set/(rho g) + v^2/(2g) with v from the previous EPANET run in the pipe on that port until the setting changes by < 1e-12 m.",
